{"step_index":68,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T07:49:06Z","content":"Based on your new syllabus and the PYQ analysis, here is the exact list of derivations you need to know. \n\nI have split them into **Tier 1 (Must-Do)** and **Tier 2 (Do if you have time)**.\n\n### 🔴 Tier 1: The \"Must-Do\" Derivations (Highest Probability)\nThese are the heavy 4 to 7-mark derivations that appear repeatedly and perfectly fit a 30-mark mid-sem paper:\n\n1. **Logarithmic Decrement ($\\delta$)**\n   *   *The Question:* \"Define Logarithmic Decrement and derive its expression in terms of damping factor ($\\zeta$).\" \n   *   *(This is the absolute most important derivation in your syllabus).*\n2. **Natural Frequency by Energy or Rayleigh’s Method**\n   *   *The Question:* \"Derive the expression for the natural frequency of free longitudinal vibration using the Energy Method (or Rayleigh's Method).\"\n3. **Piston Effort to Turning Moment (Crank Effort)**\n   *   *The Question:* \"Derive the expression of turning moment at the crankshaft in terms of piston effort ($F_p$) and angle turned by the crank ($\\theta$).\"\n\n### 🟡 Tier 2: The \"Backup\" Derivations (Secondary Probability)\nIf the professor wants to give a slightly tougher paper, they will pull one of these:\n\n4. **Equation of Motion for a Damped System**\n   *   *The Question:* \"Derive the expression for the equation of motion of a Critically-damped system (or Under-damped system).\"\n5. **Torsional Vibration of a Two-Rotor System**\n   *   *The Question:* \"Derive the expression for the natural frequency of torsional vibration of a shaft carrying two rotors (and find the position of the node).\"\n6. **Dynamically Equivalent System**\n   *   *The Question:* \"State and prove the three necessary conditions to replace a rigid body with a dynamically equivalent system of two masses.\"\n\n**Your Strategy right now:** \nTake a blank piece of paper. Do not look at a book. Try to write out the mathematical steps for **Logarithmic Decrement** and **Rayleigh's Method** (I gave you the steps for both in the previous message). \n\nIf you can write those two smoothly, you have essentially secured a 7-mark question.","thinking":"**Prioritizing Derivations List**\n\nI'm now focusing on generating that comprehensive, prioritized list of all the DOM derivations. I've considered that the user needs the *full* list, so I'm aiming to be as complete as possible. It is coming along.\n\n\n"}
